# Per-deployment context written by 10-provision.ps1; contains the
# operator's Azure subscription ID and other resource IDs.
.context.json
# Regenerated ACI deployment file written by 20-build-and-deploy.ps1;
# contains live ACR credentials, never commit.
.aci-deploy.yaml
# Local-only state written by 40-ladder.ps1 / 21-reconfigure.ps1.
.fleet-size.config
# Per-rung sweep results written by 40-ladder.ps1. Local-only,
# possibly contains throughput numbers from cost-sensitive runs.
.ladder-results.csv
.ladder-phaseA.csv
# Per-operator BENCH_PREFIX persisted by 10-provision.ps1. Random per machine,
# used to keep storage-account / ACR names globally unique. Never commit.
.prefix
# Ephemeral per-probe driver scripts, manifests, and run logs written by
# the operator while iterating on a scaling.md probe series (e.g.
# `.run-U9g-driver.ps1`, `.run-U9hA-manifest.csv`). The shape that
# actually shipped is documented in scaling.md; the local drivers are
# not reusable tooling. The conventional `40-ladder.ps1` and friends
# remain tracked.
.run-*
# Per-probe sweep directories written by 40-ladder.ps1 when copying a
# rung's CSVs and logs aside for a single scaling.md probe (e.g.
# `.u9h-d-sweep/`, `.u9j-rung-sweep/`). The directory contents - CSVs,
# logs, and any other captured evidence - are intentionally local-only.
# `*.log` is already covered by the top-level rule, but the CSVs inside
# (renamed to `.results.csv` / `.phaseA.csv` per directory) are not,
# so we ignore the whole directory shape here.
.*-sweep/